  {
   "xml_index": 3,
   "xml_name": "L07_003_List From A String",
   "display_name": "List From A String",
   "questiontext_html": "<p>The function <code>list(...)</code> <b>converts</b> other kinds of values into a list. Given a string, it makes a list of its characters, one item per character (spaces count too):</p>\n<pre>print(list(&quot;Goa!&quot;))\nprint(list(&quot;a b&quot;))\nprint(len(list(&quot;hello&quot;)))</pre>\n<p>Output:</p>\n<pre>[&#x27;G&#x27;, &#x27;o&#x27;, &#x27;a&#x27;, &#x27;!&#x27;]\n[&#x27;a&#x27;, &#x27; &#x27;, &#x27;b&#x27;]\n5</pre>\n<p><b>Your task:</b> write the function <code>letters(word)</code>, which returns the list of characters of the string <code>word</code>. The empty string <code>\"\"</code> gives the empty list.</p>\n<p>For example, <code>letters(\"abc\")</code> returns <code>['a', 'b', 'c']</code>. (Python prints strings inside a list with single quotes.)</p>",
   "answerpreload": "def letters(word):\n    # write your code here\n\n\n# ---- Use this space to test your function; comment it out before Check ----\n# print(letters(\"abc\"))\n",
   "mark": 1.0,
   "tests": [
    {
     "testcode": "print(letters(\"abc\"))",
     "stdin": "",
     "expected": "['a', 'b', 'c']",
     "extra": "",
     "show": true,
     "example": true,
     "in_precheck": true,
     "in_check": true
    },
    {
     "testcode": "print(letters(\"Goa\"))",
     "stdin": "",
     "expected": "['G', 'o', 'a']",
     "extra": "",
     "show": true,
     "example": true,
     "in_precheck": false,
     "in_check": true
    },
    {
     "testcode": "print(letters(\"\"))",
