  {
   "xml_index": 8,
   "xml_name": "L07_008_Middle Item",
   "display_name": "Middle Item",
   "questiontext_html": "<p>An index can be any expression that gives an integer, such as <code>L[len(L) - 1]</code> (the last item) or <code>L[n // 2]</code>.</p>\n<p>For a list with an <b>odd</b> number of items, the middle item is at index <code>len(L) // 2</code>. For example, a list of 7 items has indexes 0 to 6, and <code>7 // 2</code> is 3:</p>\n<table style=\"border-collapse:separate;border-spacing:2px 0;margin:6px 0 4px\"><tr><td style=\"padding-right:10px;white-space:nowrap;font-family:monospace\">L =</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:5px 7px;white-space:nowrap;font-family:monospace;font-size:14px;background:#e2e6ea;color:#8a939c;border-radius:2px\">&#x27;a&#x27;</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:5px 7px;white-space:nowrap;font-family:monospace;font-size:14px;background:#e2e6ea;color:#8a939c;border-radius:2px\">&#x27;b&#x27;</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:5px 7px;white-space:nowrap;font-family:monospace;font-size:14px;background:#e2e6ea;color:#8a939c;border-radius:2px\">&#x27;c&#x27;</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:5px 7px;white-space:nowrap;font-family:monospace;font-size:14px;background:rgb(52,129,188);color:#fff;border-radius:2px\">&#x27;d&#x27;</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:5px 7px;white-space:nowrap;font-family:monospace;font-size:14px;background:#e2e6ea;color:#8a939c;border-radius:2px\">&#x27;e&#x27;</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:5px 7px;white-space:nowrap;font-family:monospace;font-size:14px;background:#e2e6ea;color:#8a939c;border-radius:2px\">&#x27;f&#x27;</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:5px 7px;white-space:nowrap;font-family:monospace;font-size:14px;background:#e2e6ea;color:#8a939c;border-radius:2px\">&#x27;g&#x27;</td></tr><tr><td style=\"padding-right:10px\"></td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:1px 6px;font-size:12px;color:#8a939c\">0</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:1px 6px;font-size:12px;color:#8a939c\">1</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:1px 6px;font-size:12px;color:#8a939c\">2</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:1px 6px;font-size:12px;color:#8a939c\">3</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:1px 6px;font-size:12px;color:#8a939c\">4</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:1px 6px;font-size:12px;color:#8a939c\">5</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:1px 6px;font-size:12px;color:#8a939c\">6</td></tr></table><div style=\"font-size:13px;color:#8a939c;margin:0 0 10px\">len(L) is 7, and 7 // 2 is 3</div>\n<p><b>Your task:</b> write the function <code>middle(L)</code>, which returns the middle item of a list <code>L</code> with an odd number of items.</p>\n<p>For example, <code>middle([1, 2, 3])</code> returns <code>2</code>.</p>",
   "answerpreload": "def middle(L):\n    # write your code here\n\n\n# ---- Use this space to test your function; comment it out before Check ----\n# print(middle([1, 2, 3]))\n",
   "mark": 1.0,
   "tests": [
    {
     "testcode": "print(middle([1, 2, 3]))",
     "stdin": "",
     "expected": "2",
