   "xml_index": 13,
   "xml_name": "L07_013_Following A Path Of Indexes",
   "display_name": "Following A Path Of Indexes",
   "questiontext_html": "<p>Lists can be nested more than one level deep. Each <code>[ ]</code> goes <b>one level further in</b>:</p>\n<pre>L = [&quot;a&quot;, &quot;b&quot;, [&quot;cc&quot;, &quot;dd&quot;, [&quot;eee&quot;, &quot;fff&quot;]], &quot;g&quot;, &quot;h&quot;]</pre>\n<table style=\"border-collapse:separate;border-spacing:2px 0;margin:6px 0 4px\"><tr><td style=\"padding-right:10px\"></td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:1px 6px;font-size:12px;color:#8a939c\">-5</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:1px 6px;font-size:12px;color:#8a939c\">-4</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:1px 6px;font-size:12px;color:#8a939c\">-3</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:1px 6px;font-size:12px;color:#8a939c\">-2</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:1px 6px;font-size:12px;color:#8a939c\">-1</td></tr><tr><td style=\"padding-right:10px;white-space:nowrap;font-family:monospace\">L =</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:5px 7px;white-space:nowrap;font-family:monospace;font-size:14px;background:#e2e6ea;color:#8a939c;border-radius:2px\">&#x27;a&#x27;</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:5px 7px;white-space:nowrap;font-family:monospace;font-size:14px;background:#e2e6ea;color:#8a939c;border-radius:2px\">&#x27;b&#x27;</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:5px 7px;white-space:nowrap;font-family:monospace;font-size:14px;background:rgb(52,129,188);color:#fff;border-radius:2px\">[...]</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:5px 7px;white-space:nowrap;font-family:monospace;font-size:14px;background:#e2e6ea;color:#8a939c;border-radius:2px\">&#x27;g&#x27;</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:5px 7px;white-space:nowrap;font-family:monospace;font-size:14px;background:#e2e6ea;color:#8a939c;border-radius:2px\">&#x27;h&#x27;</td></tr><tr><td style=\"padding-right:10px\"></td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:1px 6px;font-size:12px;color:#8a939c\">0</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:1px 6px;font-size:12px;color:#8a939c\">1</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:1px 6px;font-size:12px;color:#8a939c\">2</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:1px 6px;font-size:12px;color:#8a939c\">3</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:1px 6px;font-size:12px;color:#8a939c\">4</td></tr></table>\n<table style=\"border-collapse:separate;border-spacing:2px 0;margin:6px 0 4px\"><tr><td style=\"padding-right:10px\"></td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:1px 6px;font-size:12px;color:#8a939c\">-3</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:1px 6px;font-size:12px;color:#8a939c\">-2</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:1px 6px;font-size:12px;color:#8a939c\">-1</td></tr><tr><td style=\"padding-right:10px;white-space:nowrap;font-family:monospace\">L[2] =</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:5px 7px;white-space:nowrap;font-family:monospace;font-size:14px;background:#e2e6ea;color:#8a939c;border-radius:2px\">&#x27;cc&#x27;</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:5px 7px;white-space:nowrap;font-family:monospace;font-size:14px;background:#e2e6ea;color:#8a939c;border-radius:2px\">&#x27;dd&#x27;</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:5px 7px;white-space:nowrap;font-family:monospace;font-size:14px;background:rgb(74,163,223);color:#fff;border-radius:2px\">[...]</td></tr><tr><td style=\"padding-right:10px\"></td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:1px 6px;font-size:12px;color:#8a939c\">0</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:1px 6px;font-size:12px;color:#8a939c\">1</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:1px 6px;font-size:12px;color:#8a939c\">2</td></tr></table>\n<table style=\"border-collapse:separate;border-spacing:2px 0;margin:6px 0 4px\"><tr><td style=\"padding-right:10px\"></td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:1px 6px;font-size:12px;color:#8a939c\">-2</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:1px 6px;font-size:12px;color:#8a939c\">-1</td></tr><tr><td style=\"padding-right:10px;white-space:nowrap;font-family:monospace\">L[2][2] =</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:5px 7px;white-space:nowrap;font-family:monospace;font-size:14px;background:rgb(31,95,153);color:#fff;border-radius:2px\">&#x27;eee&#x27;</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:5px 7px;white-space:nowrap;font-family:monospace;font-size:14px;background:#e2e6ea;color:#8a939c;border-radius:2px\">&#x27;fff&#x27;</td></tr><tr><td style=\"padding-right:10px\"></td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:1px 6px;font-size:12px;color:#8a939c\">0</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:1px 6px;font-size:12px;color:#8a939c\">1</td></tr></table><div style=\"font-size:13px;color:#8a939c;margin:0 0 10px\">L[2][2][0] is &#x27;eee&#x27;</div>\n<pre>L = [&quot;a&quot;, &quot;b&quot;, [&quot;cc&quot;, &quot;dd&quot;, [&quot;eee&quot;, &quot;fff&quot;]], &quot;g&quot;, &quot;h&quot;]\nprint(L[2])\nprint(L[2][2])\nprint(L[2][2][0])</pre>\n<p>Output:</p>\n<pre>[&#x27;cc&#x27;, &#x27;dd&#x27;, [&#x27;eee&#x27;, &#x27;fff&#x27;]]\n[&#x27;eee&#x27;, &#x27;fff&#x27;]\neee</pre>\n<p>A path of indexes like <code>[2, 2, 0]</code> can be followed with a loop: start with <code>item = L</code>, and for each index <code>p</code> in the path, go one level in with <code>item = item[p]</code>.</p>\n<p><b>Indentation reminder:</b> the body of an <code>if</code>, loop or function must be indented (press Tab or type 4 spaces). Only the spaces at the start of a line matter.</p>\n<p><b>Your task:</b> write the function <code>follow(L, path)</code>, where <code>path</code> is a list of indexes. It returns what you reach by indexing <code>L</code> with each index of <code>path</code> in turn. An empty path returns <code>L</code> itself. The paths are always valid.</p>\n<p>For example, <code>follow([\"a\", \"b\", [\"cc\", \"dd\", [\"eee\", \"fff\"]], \"g\", \"h\"], [2, 2, 0])</code> returns <code>'eee'</code>.</p>",
   "answerpreload": "def follow(L, path):\n    # write your code here\n\n\n# ---- Use this space to test your function; comment it out before Check ----\n# print(follow([\"a\", \"b\", [\"cc\", \"dd\", [\"eee\", \"fff\"]], \"g\", \"h\"], [2, 2, 0]))\n",
   "mark": 1.0,
   "tests": [
    {
     "testcode": "L = [\"a\", \"b\", [\"cc\", \"dd\", [\"eee\", \"fff\"]], \"g\", \"h\"]\nprint(follow(L, [2, 2, 0]))",
     "stdin": "",
     "expected": "eee",
     "extra": "",
     "show": true,
     "example": true,
     "in_precheck": true,
     "in_check": true
    },
    {
     "testcode": "L = [\"a\", \"b\", [\"cc\", \"dd\", [\"eee\", \"fff\"]], \"g\", \"h\"]\nprint(follow(L, [1]))",
     "stdin": "",
     "expected": "b",
     "extra": "",
     "show": true,
     "example": true,
     "in_precheck": false,
     "in_check": true
    },
    {
     "testcode": "L = [\"a\", \"b\", [\"cc\", \"dd\", [\"eee\", \"fff\"]], \"g\", \"h\"]\nprint(follow(L, [2, 1]))",
     "stdin": "",
     "expected": "dd",
     "extra": "",
     "show": true,
     "example": true,
     "in_precheck": false,
     "in_check": true
    },
    {
     "testcode": "L = [\"a\", \"b\", [\"cc\", \"dd\", [\"eee\", \"fff\"]], \"g\", \"h\"]\nprint(follow(L, [2, -1, -1]))",
     "stdin": "",
