  {
   "xml_index": 14,
   "xml_name": "L07_014_Slice From Start To Stop",
   "display_name": "Slice From Start To Stop",
   "questiontext_html": "<p>A <b>slice</b> takes a part of a list and gives it as a <b>new list</b>. The syntax is:</p>\n<pre>L[start:stop]</pre>\n<p>It takes the items from index <code>start</code> <b>up to, but not including</b>, index <code>stop</code>, just like <code>range(start, stop)</code>. Think of the indexes as marking the <b>gaps before</b> each item: the slice runs from the gap at <code>start</code> to the gap at <code>stop</code>.</p>\n<table style=\"border-collapse:separate;border-spacing:2px 0;margin:6px 0 4px\"><tr><td style=\"padding-right:10px;white-space:nowrap;font-family:monospace\">L =</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:5px 7px;white-space:nowrap;font-family:monospace;font-size:14px;background:rgb(31,95,153);color:#fff;border-radius:2px\">&#x27;a&#x27;</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:5px 7px;white-space:nowrap;font-family:monospace;font-size:14px;background:rgb(36,104,162);color:#fff;border-radius:2px\">&#x27;b&#x27;</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:5px 7px;white-space:nowrap;font-family:monospace;font-size:14px;background:rgb(42,112,170);color:#fff;border-radius:2px\">&#x27;c&#x27;</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:5px 7px;white-space:nowrap;font-family:monospace;font-size:14px;background:rgb(47,120,179);color:#fff;border-radius:2px\">&#x27;d&#x27;</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:5px 7px;white-space:nowrap;font-family:monospace;font-size:14px;background:rgb(52,129,188);color:#fff;border-radius:2px\">&#x27;e&#x27;</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:5px 7px;white-space:nowrap;font-family:monospace;font-size:14px;background:rgb(58,138,197);color:#fff;border-radius:2px\">&#x27;f&#x27;</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:5px 7px;white-space:nowrap;font-family:monospace;font-size:14px;background:rgb(63,146,206);color:#fff;border-radius:2px\">&#x27;g&#x27;</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:5px 7px;white-space:nowrap;font-family:monospace;font-size:14px;background:rgb(69,154,214);color:#fff;border-radius:2px\">&#x27;h&#x27;</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:5px 7px;white-space:nowrap;font-family:monospace;font-size:14px;background:rgb(74,163,223);color:#fff;border-radius:2px\">&#x27;i&#x27;</td></tr><tr><td style=\"padding-right:10px\"></td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:1px 6px;font-size:12px;color:#8a939c\">0</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:1px 6px;font-size:12px;color:#8a939c\">1</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:1px 6px;font-size:12px;color:#8a939c\">2</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:1px 6px;font-size:12px;color:#8a939c\">3</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:1px 6px;font-size:12px;color:#8a939c\">4</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:1px 6px;font-size:12px;color:#8a939c\">5</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:1px 6px;font-size:12px;color:#8a939c\">6</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:1px 6px;font-size:12px;color:#8a939c\">7</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:1px 6px;font-size:12px;color:#8a939c\">8</td></tr></table>\n<table style=\"border-collapse:separate;border-spacing:2px 0;margin:6px 0 4px\"><tr><td style=\"padding-right:10px;white-space:nowrap;font-family:monospace\">L[2:7] =</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:5px 7px;white-space:nowrap;font-family:monospace;font-size:14px;background:#e2e6ea;color:#8a939c;border-radius:2px\">&#x27;a&#x27;</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:5px 7px;white-space:nowrap;font-family:monospace;font-size:14px;background:#e2e6ea;color:#8a939c;border-radius:2px\">&#x27;b&#x27;</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:5px 7px;white-space:nowrap;font-family:monospace;font-size:14px;background:rgb(42,112,170);color:#fff;border-radius:2px\">&#x27;c&#x27;</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:5px 7px;white-space:nowrap;font-family:monospace;font-size:14px;background:rgb(47,120,179);color:#fff;border-radius:2px\">&#x27;d&#x27;</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:5px 7px;white-space:nowrap;font-family:monospace;font-size:14px;background:rgb(52,129,188);color:#fff;border-radius:2px\">&#x27;e&#x27;</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:5px 7px;white-space:nowrap;font-family:monospace;font-size:14px;background:rgb(58,138,197);color:#fff;border-radius:2px\">&#x27;f&#x27;</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:5px 7px;white-space:nowrap;font-family:monospace;font-size:14px;background:rgb(63,146,206);color:#fff;border-radius:2px\">&#x27;g&#x27;</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:5px 7px;white-space:nowrap;font-family:monospace;font-size:14px;background:#e2e6ea;color:#8a939c;border-radius:2px\">&#x27;h&#x27;</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:5px 7px;white-space:nowrap;font-family:monospace;font-size:14px;background:#e2e6ea;color:#8a939c;border-radius:2px\">&#x27;i&#x27;</td></tr><tr><td style=\"padding-right:10px\"></td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:1px 6px;font-size:12px;color:#8a939c\">0</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:1px 6px;font-size:12px;color:#8a939c\">1</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:1px 6px;font-size:12px;color:#8a939c\">2</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:1px 6px;font-size:12px;color:#8a939c\">3</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:1px 6px;font-size:12px;color:#8a939c\">4</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:1px 6px;font-size:12px;color:#8a939c\">5</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:1px 6px;font-size:12px;color:#8a939c\">6</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:1px 6px;font-size:12px;color:#8a939c\">7</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:1px 6px;font-size:12px;color:#8a939c\">8</td></tr><tr><td style=\"padding-right:10px\"></td><td style=\"text-align:center;font-size:12px;color:#16202b;white-space:nowrap\"></td><td style=\"text-align:center;font-size:12px;color:#16202b;white-space:nowrap\"></td><td style=\"text-align:center;font-size:12px;color:#2e7a48;white-space:nowrap\">&uarr;<br>start</td><td style=\"text-align:center;font-size:12px;color:#16202b;white-space:nowrap\"></td><td style=\"text-align:center;font-size:12px;color:#16202b;white-space:nowrap\"></td><td style=\"text-align:center;font-size:12px;color:#16202b;white-space:nowrap\"></td><td style=\"text-align:center;font-size:12px;color:#16202b;white-space:nowrap\"></td><td style=\"text-align:center;font-size:12px;color:#7b3fa0;white-space:nowrap\">&uarr;<br>stop</td><td style=\"text-align:center;font-size:12px;color:#16202b;white-space:nowrap\"></td></tr></table><div style=\"font-size:13px;color:#8a939c;margin:0 0 10px\">start 2 is included; stop 7 is not</div>\n<p>So <code>L[2:7]</code> is <code>['c', 'd', 'e', 'f', 'g']</code>: 5 items, which is <code>stop - start</code>. If <code>start</code> and <code>stop</code> are equal, the slice is empty. The original list does not change.</p>\n<pre>L = [&quot;a&quot;, &quot;b&quot;, &quot;c&quot;, &quot;d&quot;, &quot;e&quot;, &quot;f&quot;, &quot;g&quot;, &quot;h&quot;, &quot;i&quot;]\nprint(L[2:7])\nprint(L[0:2])\nprint(L[4:4])\nprint(L)</pre>\n<p>Output:</p>\n<pre>[&#x27;c&#x27;, &#x27;d&#x27;, &#x27;e&#x27;, &#x27;f&#x27;, &#x27;g&#x27;]\n[&#x27;a&#x27;, &#x27;b&#x27;]\n[]\n[&#x27;a&#x27;, &#x27;b&#x27;, &#x27;c&#x27;, &#x27;d&#x27;, &#x27;e&#x27;, &#x27;f&#x27;, &#x27;g&#x27;, &#x27;h&#x27;, &#x27;i&#x27;]</pre>\n<p><b>Your task:</b> write the function <code>part(L, a, b)</code>, which returns the slice of <code>L</code> from index <code>a</code> up to (not including) index <code>b</code>. The indexes satisfy <code>0 &lt;= a &lt;= b &lt;= len(L)</code>.</p>\n<p>For example, <code>part([10, 20, 30, 40, 50], 1, 3)</code> returns <code>[20, 30]</code>.</p>",
   "answerpreload": "def part(L, a, b):\n    # write your code here\n\n\n# ---- Use this space to test your function; comment it out before Check ----\n# print(part([10, 20, 30, 40, 50], 1, 3))\n",
   "mark": 1.0,
