  {
   "xml_index": 17,
   "xml_name": "L07_017_Every Other Item",
   "display_name": "Every Other Item",
   "questiontext_html": "<p>A slice can have a third part, the <b>step</b>: <code>L[start:stop:step]</code> takes every <code>step</code>-th item. The step works like the step of <code>range</code>.</p>\n<table style=\"border-collapse:separate;border-spacing:2px 0;margin:6px 0 4px\"><tr><td style=\"padding-right:10px;white-space:nowrap;font-family:monospace\">L[2:7:2] =</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:5px 7px;white-space:nowrap;font-family:monospace;font-size:14px;background:#e2e6ea;color:#8a939c;border-radius:2px\">&#x27;a&#x27;</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:5px 7px;white-space:nowrap;font-family:monospace;font-size:14px;background:#e2e6ea;color:#8a939c;border-radius:2px\">&#x27;b&#x27;</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:5px 7px;white-space:nowrap;font-family:monospace;font-size:14px;background:rgb(42,112,170);color:#fff;border-radius:2px\">&#x27;c&#x27;</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:5px 7px;white-space:nowrap;font-family:monospace;font-size:14px;background:#e2e6ea;color:#8a939c;border-radius:2px\">&#x27;d&#x27;</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:5px 7px;white-space:nowrap;font-family:monospace;font-size:14px;background:rgb(52,129,188);color:#fff;border-radius:2px\">&#x27;e&#x27;</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:5px 7px;white-space:nowrap;font-family:monospace;font-size:14px;background:#e2e6ea;color:#8a939c;border-radius:2px\">&#x27;f&#x27;</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:5px 7px;white-space:nowrap;font-family:monospace;font-size:14px;background:rgb(63,146,206);color:#fff;border-radius:2px\">&#x27;g&#x27;</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:5px 7px;white-space:nowrap;font-family:monospace;font-size:14px;background:#e2e6ea;color:#8a939c;border-radius:2px\">&#x27;h&#x27;</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:5px 7px;white-space:nowrap;font-family:monospace;font-size:14px;background:#e2e6ea;color:#8a939c;border-radius:2px\">&#x27;i&#x27;</td></tr><tr><td style=\"padding-right:10px\"></td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:1px 6px;font-size:12px;color:#8a939c\">0</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:1px 6px;font-size:12px;color:#8a939c\">1</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:1px 6px;font-size:12px;color:#8a939c\">2</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:1px 6px;font-size:12px;color:#8a939c\">3</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:1px 6px;font-size:12px;color:#8a939c\">4</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:1px 6px;font-size:12px;color:#8a939c\">5</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:1px 6px;font-size:12px;color:#8a939c\">6</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:1px 6px;font-size:12px;color:#8a939c\">7</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:1px 6px;font-size:12px;color:#8a939c\">8</td></tr><tr><td style=\"padding-right:10px\"></td><td style=\"text-align:center;font-size:12px;color:#16202b;white-space:nowrap\"></td><td style=\"text-align:center;font-size:12px;color:#16202b;white-space:nowrap\"></td><td style=\"text-align:center;font-size:12px;color:#2e7a48;white-space:nowrap\">&uarr;<br>start</td><td style=\"text-align:center;font-size:12px;color:#16202b;white-space:nowrap\"></td><td style=\"text-align:center;font-size:12px;color:#16202b;white-space:nowrap\"></td><td style=\"text-align:center;font-size:12px;color:#16202b;white-space:nowrap\"></td><td style=\"text-align:center;font-size:12px;color:#16202b;white-space:nowrap\"></td><td style=\"text-align:center;font-size:12px;color:#7b3fa0;white-space:nowrap\">&uarr;<br>stop</td><td style=\"text-align:center;font-size:12px;color:#16202b;white-space:nowrap\"></td></tr></table><div style=\"font-size:13px;color:#8a939c;margin:0 0 10px\">step 2: take &#x27;c&#x27;, skip one, take &#x27;e&#x27;, skip one, take &#x27;g&#x27;</div>\n<p>Parts can still be left out: <code>L[::2]</code> takes every second item from the start (indexes 0, 2, 4, ...), and <code>L[1::2]</code> every second item starting at index 1.</p>\n<pre>L = [&quot;a&quot;, &quot;b&quot;, &quot;c&quot;, &quot;d&quot;, &quot;e&quot;, &quot;f&quot;, &quot;g&quot;, &quot;h&quot;, &quot;i&quot;]\nprint(L[2:7:2])\nprint(L[::2])\nprint(L[1::2])\nprint(L[::3])</pre>\n<p>Output:</p>\n<pre>[&#x27;c&#x27;, &#x27;e&#x27;, &#x27;g&#x27;]\n[&#x27;a&#x27;, &#x27;c&#x27;, &#x27;e&#x27;, &#x27;g&#x27;, &#x27;i&#x27;]\n[&#x27;b&#x27;, &#x27;d&#x27;, &#x27;f&#x27;, &#x27;h&#x27;]\n[&#x27;a&#x27;, &#x27;d&#x27;, &#x27;g&#x27;]</pre>\n<p><b>Your task:</b> write two functions, for any list <code>L</code>:</p>\n<ul><li><code>even_positions(L)</code> returns the items at indexes 0, 2, 4, ...;</li><li><code>odd_positions(L)</code> returns the items at indexes 1, 3, 5, ...</li></ul>\n<p>For example, <code>even_positions([10, 11, 12, 13, 14])</code> returns <code>[10, 12, 14]</code> and <code>odd_positions([10, 11, 12, 13, 14])</code> returns <code>[11, 13]</code>.</p>",
   "answerpreload": "def even_positions(L):\n    # write your code here\n\n\ndef odd_positions(L):\n    # write your code here\n\n\n# ---- Use this space to test your function; comment it out before Check ----\n# print(even_positions([10, 11, 12, 13, 14]))\n# print(odd_positions([10, 11, 12, 13, 14]))\n",
   "mark": 1.0,
   "tests": [
