  {
   "xml_index": 21,
   "xml_name": "L07_021_Rotate A List",
   "display_name": "Rotate A List",
   "questiontext_html": "<p>Two slices and <code>+</code> (which joins two lists into a new one) can <b>rotate</b> a list: move the first <code>k</code> items to the back.</p>\n<table style=\"border-collapse:separate;border-spacing:2px 0;margin:6px 0 4px\"><tr><td style=\"padding-right:10px;white-space:nowrap;font-family:monospace\">L =</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:5px 7px;white-space:nowrap;font-family:monospace;font-size:14px;background:#e2e6ea;color:#8a939c;border-radius:2px\">&#x27;a&#x27;</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:5px 7px;white-space:nowrap;font-family:monospace;font-size:14px;background:#e2e6ea;color:#8a939c;border-radius:2px\">&#x27;b&#x27;</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:5px 7px;white-space:nowrap;font-family:monospace;font-size:14px;background:rgb(52,129,188);color:#fff;border-radius:2px\">&#x27;c&#x27;</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:5px 7px;white-space:nowrap;font-family:monospace;font-size:14px;background:rgb(63,146,206);color:#fff;border-radius:2px\">&#x27;d&#x27;</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:5px 7px;white-space:nowrap;font-family:monospace;font-size:14px;background:rgb(74,163,223);color:#fff;border-radius:2px\">&#x27;e&#x27;</td></tr><tr><td style=\"padding-right:10px\"></td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:1px 6px;font-size:12px;color:#8a939c\">0</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:1px 6px;font-size:12px;color:#8a939c\">1</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:1px 6px;font-size:12px;color:#8a939c\">2</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:1px 6px;font-size:12px;color:#8a939c\">3</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:1px 6px;font-size:12px;color:#8a939c\">4</td></tr><tr><td style=\"padding-right:10px\"></td><td style=\"text-align:center;font-size:12px;color:#16202b;white-space:nowrap\"></td><td style=\"text-align:center;font-size:12px;color:#16202b;white-space:nowrap\"></td><td style=\"text-align:center;font-size:12px;color:#16202b;white-space:nowrap\">&uarr;<br>k</td><td style=\"text-align:center;font-size:12px;color:#16202b;white-space:nowrap\"></td><td style=\"text-align:center;font-size:12px;color:#16202b;white-space:nowrap\"></td></tr></table><div style=\"font-size:13px;color:#8a939c;margin:0 0 10px\">k = 2: L[2:] is [&#x27;c&#x27;, &#x27;d&#x27;, &#x27;e&#x27;] and L[:2] is [&#x27;a&#x27;, &#x27;b&#x27;]</div>\n<table style=\"border-collapse:separate;border-spacing:2px 0;margin:6px 0 4px\"><tr><td style=\"padding-right:10px;white-space:nowrap;font-family:monospace\">L[2:] + L[:2] =</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:5px 7px;white-space:nowrap;font-family:monospace;font-size:14px;background:rgb(31,95,153);color:#fff;border-radius:2px\">&#x27;c&#x27;</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:5px 7px;white-space:nowrap;font-family:monospace;font-size:14px;background:rgb(42,112,170);color:#fff;border-radius:2px\">&#x27;d&#x27;</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:5px 7px;white-space:nowrap;font-family:monospace;font-size:14px;background:rgb(52,129,188);color:#fff;border-radius:2px\">&#x27;e&#x27;</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:5px 7px;white-space:nowrap;font-family:monospace;font-size:14px;background:rgb(63,146,206);color:#fff;border-radius:2px\">&#x27;a&#x27;</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:5px 7px;white-space:nowrap;font-family:monospace;font-size:14px;background:rgb(74,163,223);color:#fff;border-radius:2px\">&#x27;b&#x27;</td></tr></table>\n<p><b>Your task:</b> write the function <code>rotate_left(L, k)</code>, which returns a new list: the items of <code>L</code> moved <code>k</code> places to the left, with the first <code>k</code> items going to the back. <code>k</code> is an integer from 0 to <code>len(L)</code>.</p>\n<p>For example, <code>rotate_left([\"a\", \"b\", \"c\", \"d\", \"e\"], 2)</code> returns <code>['c', 'd', 'e', 'a', 'b']</code>.</p>",
   "answerpreload": "def rotate_left(L, k):\n    # write your code here\n\n\n# ---- Use this space to test your function; comment it out before Check ----\n# print(rotate_left([\"a\", \"b\", \"c\", \"d\", \"e\"], 2))\n",
   "mark": 1.0,
   "tests": [
    {
     "testcode": "print(rotate_left([\"a\", \"b\", \"c\", \"d\", \"e\"], 2))",
     "stdin": "",
     "expected": "['c', 'd', 'e', 'a', 'b']",
     "extra": "",
     "show": true,
     "example": true,
     "in_precheck": true,
     "in_check": true
    },
    {
     "testcode": "print(rotate_left([1, 2, 3], 0))",
     "stdin": "",
     "expected": "[1, 2, 3]",
     "extra": "",
