  {
   "xml_index": 28,
   "xml_name": "L07_028_Insert At A Position",
   "display_name": "Insert At A Position",
   "questiontext_html": "<p><code>L.insert(i, x)</code> puts <code>x</code> <b>at index <code>i</code></b>. The item that was at <code>i</code>, and all items after it, <b>shift one place to the right</b>:</p>\n<table style=\"border-collapse:separate;border-spacing:2px 0;margin:6px 0 4px\"><tr><td style=\"padding-right:10px;white-space:nowrap;font-family:monospace\">before:</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:5px 7px;white-space:nowrap;font-family:monospace;font-size:14px;background:rgb(31,95,153);color:#fff;border-radius:2px\">&#x27;red&#x27;</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:5px 7px;white-space:nowrap;font-family:monospace;font-size:14px;background:rgb(52,129,188);color:#fff;border-radius:2px\">&#x27;green&#x27;</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:5px 7px;white-space:nowrap;font-family:monospace;font-size:14px;background:rgb(74,163,223);color:#fff;border-radius:2px\">&#x27;blue&#x27;</td></tr><tr><td style=\"padding-right:10px\"></td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:1px 6px;font-size:12px;color:#8a939c\">0</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:1px 6px;font-size:12px;color:#8a939c\">1</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:1px 6px;font-size:12px;color:#8a939c\">2</td></tr></table>\n<table style=\"border-collapse:separate;border-spacing:2px 0;margin:6px 0 4px\"><tr><td style=\"padding-right:10px;white-space:nowrap;font-family:monospace\">L.insert(1, &#x27;yellow&#x27;):</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:5px 7px;white-space:nowrap;font-family:monospace;font-size:14px;background:#e2e6ea;color:#8a939c;border-radius:2px\">&#x27;red&#x27;</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:5px 7px;white-space:nowrap;font-family:monospace;font-size:14px;background:rgb(45,118,176);color:#fff;border-radius:2px\">&#x27;yellow&#x27;</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:5px 7px;white-space:nowrap;font-family:monospace;font-size:14px;background:#e2e6ea;color:#8a939c;border-radius:2px\">&#x27;green&#x27;</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:5px 7px;white-space:nowrap;font-family:monospace;font-size:14px;background:#e2e6ea;color:#8a939c;border-radius:2px\">&#x27;blue&#x27;</td></tr><tr><td style=\"padding-right:10px\"></td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:1px 6px;font-size:12px;color:#8a939c\">0</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:1px 6px;font-size:12px;color:#8a939c\">1</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:1px 6px;font-size:12px;color:#8a939c\">2</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:1px 6px;font-size:12px;color:#8a939c\">3</td></tr></table><div style=\"font-size:13px;color:#8a939c;margin:0 0 10px\">&#x27;green&#x27; and &#x27;blue&#x27; moved from 1, 2 to 2, 3</div>\n<p><code>L.insert(0, x)</code> puts <code>x</code> at the front, and <code>L.insert(len(L), x)</code> at the end (the same as <code>append</code>). Like <code>append</code>, <code>insert</code> changes the list and returns <code>None</code>.</p>\n<pre>L = [&quot;red&quot;, &quot;green&quot;, &quot;blue&quot;]\nL.insert(1, &quot;yellow&quot;)\nprint(L)\nL.insert(0, &quot;white&quot;)\nprint(L)</pre>\n<p>Output:</p>\n<pre>[&#x27;red&#x27;, &#x27;yellow&#x27;, &#x27;green&#x27;, &#x27;blue&#x27;]\n[&#x27;white&#x27;, &#x27;red&#x27;, &#x27;yellow&#x27;, &#x27;green&#x27;, &#x27;blue&#x27;]</pre>\n<p><b>Your task:</b> write the function <code>insert_sorted(L, x)</code>. The list <code>L</code> of integers is sorted from small to large; insert <code>x</code> at the right place so that <code>L</code> stays sorted (if <code>x</code> equals some items, it may go before or after them). It changes <code>L</code> and returns nothing. <code>L</code> may be empty.</p>\n<p>Hint: find the first index <code>i</code> where <code>L[i] &gt;= x</code> (or <code>len(L)</code> if there is none), then insert there.</p>\n<p>For example, after <code>L = [10, 20, 30]</code> and <code>insert_sorted(L, 25)</code>, <code>L</code> is <code>[10, 20, 25, 30]</code>.</p>",
   "answerpreload": "# Define insert_sorted(L, x): insert x into the sorted list L so it stays sorted.\n\n\n\n# ---- Use this space to test your function; comment it out before Check ----\n# L = [10, 20, 30]; insert_sorted(L, 25); print(L)\n",
   "mark": 1.0,
   "tests": [
    {
