     "example": false,
     "in_precheck": false,
     "in_check": true
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "xml_index": 32,
   "xml_name": "L07_032_Alternate Two Lists",
   "display_name": "Alternate Two Lists",
   "questiontext_html": "<p>Many list problems combine an index loop with <code>append</code>: walk through positions <code>0, 1, 2, ...</code> and build a new list from items taken from one or more lists.</p>\n<p><b>Indentation reminder:</b> the body of an <code>if</code>, loop or function must be indented (press Tab or type 4 spaces). Only the spaces at the start of a line matter.</p>\n<p><b>Your task:</b> write the function <code>interleave(a, b)</code>, which returns a new list taking items alternately from the lists <code>a</code> and <code>b</code>: <code>a[0], b[0], a[1], b[1], ...</code>. The two lists have the same length (possibly 0).</p>\n<p>For example, <code>interleave([1, 2, 3], [\"x\", \"y\", \"z\"])</code> returns <code>[1, 'x', 2, 'y', 3, 'z']</code>.</p>",
   "answerpreload": "# Define interleave(a, b).\n\n\n\n# ---- Use this space to test your function; comment it out before Check ----\n# print(interleave([1, 2, 3], [\"x\", \"y\", \"z\"]))\n",
   "mark": 1.0,
   "tests": [
    {
     "testcode": "print(interleave([1, 2, 3], [\"x\", \"y\", \"z\"]))",
     "stdin": "",
     "expected": "[1, 'x', 2, 'y', 3, 'z']",
     "extra": "",
     "show": true,
     "example": true,
     "in_precheck": true,
     "in_check": true
    },
    {
     "testcode": "print(interleave([], []))",
     "stdin": "",
     "expected": "[]",
     "extra": "",
     "show": true,
     "example": true,
     "in_precheck": false,
     "in_check": true
    },
    {
     "testcode": "print(interleave([5], [6]))",
     "stdin": "",
     "expected": "[5, 6]",
     "extra": "",
     "show": true,
     "example": true,
     "in_precheck": false,
     "in_check": true
    },
    {
     "testcode": "a = list(map(int, input().split()))\nprint(interleave(a, a[::-1]))",
     "stdin": "1 2 3 4",
     "expected": "[1, 4, 2, 3, 3, 2, 4, 1]",
     "extra": "",
     "show": false,
     "example": false,
     "in_precheck": false,
     "in_check": true
    },
    {
     "testcode": "a = list(map(int, input().split()))\nprint(interleave(a, [0] * len(a)))",
     "stdin": "9 8",
     "expected": "[9, 0, 8, 0]",
     "extra": "",
     "show": false,
     "example": false,
     "in_precheck": false,
     "in_check": true
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "xml_index": 33,
   "xml_name": "L07_033_Pop An Item",
   "display_name": "Pop An Item",
   "questiontext_html": "<p><code>L.pop(i)</code> <b>removes</b> the item at index <code>i</code> and <b>returns</b> it, so you can use it. The items after it shift one place to the left. <code>L.pop()</code> with no index removes and returns the <b>last</b> item.</p>\n<table style=\"border-collapse:separate;border-spacing:2px 0;margin:6px 0 4px\"><tr><td style=\"padding-right:10px;white-space:nowrap;font-family:monospace\">before:</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:5px 7px;white-space:nowrap;font-family:monospace;font-size:14px;background:#e2e6ea;color:#8a939c;border-radius:2px\">&#x27;a&#x27;</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:5px 7px;white-space:nowrap;font-family:monospace;font-size:14px;background:rgb(45,118,176);color:#fff;border-radius:2px\">&#x27;b&#x27;</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:5px 7px;white-space:nowrap;font-family:monospace;font-size:14px;background:#e2e6ea;color:#8a939c;border-radius:2px\">&#x27;c&#x27;</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:5px 7px;white-space:nowrap;font-family:monospace;font-size:14px;background:#e2e6ea;color:#8a939c;border-radius:2px\">&#x27;d&#x27;</td></tr><tr><td style=\"padding-right:10px\"></td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:1px 6px;font-size:12px;color:#8a939c\">0</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:1px 6px;font-size:12px;color:#8a939c\">1</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:1px 6px;font-size:12px;color:#8a939c\">2</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:1px 6px;font-size:12px;color:#8a939c\">3</td></tr></table><div style=\"font-size:13px;color:#8a939c;margin:0 0 10px\">L.pop(1) returns &#x27;b&#x27;</div>\n<table style=\"border-collapse:separate;border-spacing:2px 0;margin:6px 0 4px\"><tr><td style=\"padding-right:10px;white-space:nowrap;font-family:monospace\">after:</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:5px 7px;white-space:nowrap;font-family:monospace;font-size:14px;background:rgb(31,95,153);color:#fff;border-radius:2px\">&#x27;a&#x27;</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:5px 7px;white-space:nowrap;font-family:monospace;font-size:14px;background:rgb(52,129,188);color:#fff;border-radius:2px\">&#x27;c&#x27;</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:5px 7px;white-space:nowrap;font-family:monospace;font-size:14px;background:rgb(74,163,223);color:#fff;border-radius:2px\">&#x27;d&#x27;</td></tr><tr><td style=\"padding-right:10px\"></td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:1px 6px;font-size:12px;color:#8a939c\">0</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:1px 6px;font-size:12px;color:#8a939c\">1</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:1px 6px;font-size:12px;color:#8a939c\">2</td></tr></table>\n<pre>L = [&quot;a&quot;, &quot;b&quot;, &quot;c&quot;, &quot;d&quot;]\nx = L.pop(1)\nprint(x, L)\ny = L.pop()\nprint(y, L)</pre>\n<p>Output:</p>\n<pre>b [&#x27;a&#x27;, &#x27;c&#x27;, &#x27;d&#x27;]\nd [&#x27;a&#x27;, &#x27;c&#x27;]</pre>\n<p><b>Your task:</b> write the function <code>move_to_end(L, i)</code>, which moves the item at index <code>i</code> of the list <code>L</code> to the end of <code>L</code> (use <code>pop</code> and <code>append</code>). It changes <code>L</code> and returns nothing. <code>i</code> is a valid index.</p>\n<p>For example, after <code>L = [\"a\", \"b\", \"c\", \"d\"]</code> and <code>move_to_end(L, 1)</code>, <code>L</code> is <code>['a', 'c', 'd', 'b']</code>.</p>",
   "answerpreload": "# Define move_to_end(L, i): use pop and append; change L, return nothing.\n\n\n\n# ---- Use this space to test your function; comment it out before Check ----\n# L = [\"a\", \"b\", \"c\", \"d\"]; move_to_end(L, 1); print(L)\n",
   "mark": 1.0,
   "tests": [
    {
     "testcode": "L = [\"a\", \"b\", \"c\", \"d\"]\nmove_to_end(L, 1)\nprint(L)",
     "stdin": "",
     "expected": "['a', 'c', 'd', 'b']",
     "extra": "",
     "show": true,
     "example": true,
     "in_precheck": true,
     "in_check": true
    },
    {
     "testcode": "L = [1, 2, 3]\nmove_to_end(L, -1)\nprint(L)",
     "stdin": "",
     "expected": "[1, 2, 3]",
     "extra": "",
     "show": true,
     "example": true,
     "in_precheck": false,
     "in_check": true
    },
    {
     "testcode": "L = [9]\nmove_to_end(L, 0)\nprint(L)",
     "stdin": "",
     "expected": "[9]",
     "extra": "",
     "show": true,
     "example": true,
     "in_precheck": false,
     "in_check": true
    },
    {
     "testcode": "L = list(map(int, input().split()))\nmove_to_end(L, 0)\nprint(L)",
     "stdin": "4 5 6 7",
     "expected": "[5, 6, 7, 4]",
     "extra": "",
     "show": false,
     "example": false,
     "in_precheck": false,
     "in_check": true
    },
    {
     "testcode": "L = list(map(int, input().split()))\nmove_to_end(L, 2)\nprint(L)",
     "stdin": "1 2 3 4 5",
     "expected": "[1, 2, 4, 5, 3]",
     "extra": "",
     "show": false,
     "example": false,
     "in_precheck": false,
     "in_check": true
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "xml_index": 34,
   "xml_name": "L07_034_Delete By Index And Slice",
   "display_name": "Delete By Index And Slice",
   "questiontext_html": "<p>The <code>del</code> statement deletes by position, without returning anything:</p>\n<ul><li><code>del L[i]</code> deletes the item at index <code>i</code>;</li><li><code>del L[a:b]</code> deletes a whole <b>slice</b>.</li></ul>\n<table style=\"border-collapse:separate;border-spacing:2px 0;margin:6px 0 4px\"><tr><td style=\"padding-right:10px;white-space:nowrap;font-family:monospace\">L =</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:5px 7px;white-space:nowrap;font-family:monospace;font-size:14px;background:rgb(31,95,153);color:#fff;border-radius:2px\">&#x27;a&#x27;</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:5px 7px;white-space:nowrap;font-family:monospace;font-size:14px;background:rgb(38,106,165);color:#fff;border-radius:2px\">&#x27;b&#x27;</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:5px 7px;white-space:nowrap;font-family:monospace;font-size:14px;background:rgb(45,118,176);color:#fff;border-radius:2px\">&#x27;c&#x27;</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:5px 7px;white-space:nowrap;font-family:monospace;font-size:14px;background:#e2e6ea;color:#8a939c;border-radius:2px\">&#x27;d&#x27;</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:5px 7px;white-space:nowrap;font-family:monospace;font-size:14px;background:#e2e6ea;color:#8a939c;border-radius:2px\">&#x27;e&#x27;</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:5px 7px;white-space:nowrap;font-family:monospace;font-size:14px;background:rgb(67,152,211);color:#fff;border-radius:2px\">&#x27;f&#x27;</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:5px 7px;white-space:nowrap;font-family:monospace;font-size:14px;background:rgb(74,163,223);color:#fff;border-radius:2px\">&#x27;g&#x27;</td></tr><tr><td style=\"padding-right:10px\"></td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:1px 6px;font-size:12px;color:#8a939c\">0</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:1px 6px;font-size:12px;color:#8a939c\">1</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:1px 6px;font-size:12px;color:#8a939c\">2</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:1px 6px;font-size:12px;color:#8a939c\">3</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:1px 6px;font-size:12px;color:#8a939c\">4</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:1px 6px;font-size:12px;color:#8a939c\">5</td><td style=\"text-align:center;padding:1px 6px;font-size:12px;color:#8a939c\">6</td></tr><tr><td style=\"padding-right:10px\"></td><td style=\"text-align:center;font-size:12px;color:#16202b;white-space:nowrap\"></td><td style=\"text-align:center;font-size:12px;color:#16202b;white-space:nowrap\"></td><td style=\"text-align:center;font-size:12px;color:#16202b;white-space:nowrap\"></td><td style=\"text-align:center;font-size:12px;color:#2e7a48;white-space:nowrap\">&uarr;<br>start</td><td style=\"text-align:center;font-size:12px;color:#16202b;white-space:nowrap\"></td><td style=\"text-align:center;font-size:12px;color:#7b3fa0;white-space:nowrap\">&uarr;<br>stop</td><td style=\"text-align:center;font-size:12px;color:#16202b;white-space:nowrap\"></td></tr></table><div style=\"font-size:13px;color:#8a939c;margin:0 0 10px\">del L[3:5] removes &#x27;d&#x27; and &#x27;e&#x27;</div>\n<pre>L = [&quot;a&quot;, &quot;b&quot;, &quot;c&quot;, &quot;d&quot;, &quot;e&quot;, &quot;f&quot;, &quot;g&quot;]\ndel L[3:5]\nprint(L)\ndel L[0]\nprint(L)</pre>\n<p>Output:</p>\n<pre>[&#x27;a&#x27;, &#x27;b&#x27;, &#x27;c&#x27;, &#x27;f&#x27;, &#x27;g&#x27;]\n[&#x27;b&#x27;, &#x27;c&#x27;, &#x27;f&#x27;, &#x27;g&#x27;]</pre>\n<p><b>Careful with <code>-0</code>:</b> to delete the last <code>k</code> items you might write <code>del L[-k:]</code>, but for <code>k = 0</code> this is <code>del L[0:]</code>, which deletes <b>everything</b>! Using <code>len(L) - k</code> avoids this.</p>\n<p><b>Your task:</b> write the function <code>trim(L, k)</code>, which deletes the first <code>k</code> items and the last <code>k</code> items of the list <code>L</code>. It changes <code>L</code> and returns nothing. <code>k</code> is a non-negative integer and <code>L</code> has at least <code>2 * k</code> items.</p>\n<p>For example, after <code>L = [1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6]</code> and <code>trim(L, 2)</code>, <code>L</code> is <code>[3, 4]</code>.</p>",
   "answerpreload": "# Define trim(L, k): delete the first k and last k items of L.\n\n\n\n# ---- Use this space to test your function; comment it out before Check ----\n# L = [1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6]; trim(L, 2); print(L)\n",
   "mark": 1.0,
   "tests": [
    {
     "testcode": "L = [1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6]\ntrim(L, 2)\nprint(L)",
     "stdin": "",
     "expected": "[3, 4]",
     "extra": "",
     "show": true,
     "example": true,
     "in_precheck": true,
     "in_check": true
    },
    {
     "testcode": "L = [1, 2, 3]\ntrim(L, 0)\nprint(L)",
     "stdin": "",
     "expected": "[1, 2, 3]",
     "extra": "",
     "show": true,
     "example": true,
     "in_precheck": false,
     "in_check": true
    },
    {
     "testcode": "L = [7, 8]\ntrim(L, 1)\nprint(L)",
     "stdin": "",
     "expected": "[]",
     "extra": "",
     "show": true,
     "example": true,
     "in_precheck": false,
     "in_check": true
    },
    {
     "testcode": "L = list(map(int, input().split()))\ntrim(L, 1)\nprint(L)",
     "stdin": "10 20 30 40 50",
     "expected": "[20, 30, 40]",
     "extra": "",
     "show": false,
     "example": false,
     "in_precheck": false,
     "in_check": true
    },
    {
     "testcode": "L = list(map(int, input().split()))\ntrim(L, 3)\nprint(L)",
     "stdin": "1 2 3 4 5 6 7",
     "expected": "[4]",
     "extra": "",
     "show": false,
