  {
   "xml_index": 35,
   "xml_name": "L07_035_Remove The First Match",
   "display_name": "Remove The First Match",
   "questiontext_html": "<p><code>L.remove(x)</code> deletes by <b>value</b>: it removes the <b>first</b> item equal to <code>x</code> (only that one). If <code>x</code> is not in the list, it raises a <code>ValueError</code>, so check with <code>in</code> first when you are not sure:</p>\n<pre>L = [3, 1, 4, 1, 5]\nL.remove(1)\nprint(L)\nif 9 in L:\n    L.remove(9)\nprint(L)</pre>\n<p>Output:</p>\n<pre>[3, 4, 1, 5]\n[3, 4, 1, 5]</pre>\n<p>To sum up the ways of removing: <code>remove(x)</code> by value, <code>pop(i)</code> and <code>del L[i]</code> by index.</p>\n<p><b>Indentation reminder:</b> the body of an <code>if</code>, loop or function must be indented (press Tab or type 4 spaces). Only the spaces at the start of a line matter.</p>\n<p><b>Your task:</b> write the function <code>remove_first(L, x)</code>, which removes the first item equal to <code>x</code> from the list <code>L</code>, if there is one, and returns <code>True</code>; if <code>x</code> is not in <code>L</code>, it leaves <code>L</code> unchanged and returns <code>False</code>.</p>\n<p>For example, after <code>L = [3, 1, 4, 1, 5]</code>, <code>remove_first(L, 1)</code> returns <code>True</code> and <code>L</code> becomes <code>[3, 4, 1, 5]</code>.</p>",
   "answerpreload": "# Define remove_first(L, x): remove the first x (if any) and return True or False.\n\n\n\n# ---- Use this space to test your function; comment it out before Check ----\n# L = [3, 1, 4, 1, 5]; print(remove_first(L, 1)); print(L)\n",
   "mark": 1.0,
   "tests": [
    {
     "testcode": "L = [3, 1, 4, 1, 5]\nprint(remove_first(L, 1))\nprint(L)",
     "stdin": "",
     "expected": "True\n[3, 4, 1, 5]",
     "extra": "",
     "show": true,
     "example": true,
     "in_precheck": true,
     "in_check": true
    },
    {
     "testcode": "L = [3, 1, 4]\nprint(remove_first(L, 9))\nprint(L)",
     "stdin": "",
     "expected": "False\n[3, 1, 4]",
     "extra": "",
     "show": true,
     "example": true,
     "in_precheck": false,
     "in_check": true
    },
    {
     "testcode": "L = []\nprint(remove_first(L, 0))\nprint(L)",
     "stdin": "",
     "expected": "False\n[]",
     "extra": "",
     "show": true,
     "example": true,
     "in_precheck": false,
     "in_check": true
    },
    {
