  {
   "xml_index": 37,
   "xml_name": "L07_037_Clear Versus A New Empty List",
   "display_name": "Clear Versus A New Empty List",
   "questiontext_html": "<p>There are two ways to \"empty\" a list, and they are <b>not</b> the same:</p>\n<ul><li><code>L.clear()</code> removes all items from <b>this</b> list. Every name for this list now sees an empty list.</li><li><code>L = []</code> makes the name <code>L</code> point to a <b>new</b>, empty list. The old list is not changed, and other names for it still see all the items.</li></ul>\n<p>Inside a function this matters a lot: <code>L = []</code> only changes the function's own name <code>L</code>, and the caller's list stays full.</p>\n<p>The function below is supposed to empty the list it is given, but the caller's list stays unchanged. Fix it.</p>\n<p><b>Your task:</b> fix the function <code>reset(L)</code> so that it empties the list <code>L</code> itself (all names for that list then see <code>[]</code>). It returns nothing.</p>\n<p>For example, after <code>a = [1, 2]</code>, <code>b = a</code> and <code>reset(a)</code>, both <code>a</code> and <code>b</code> are <code>[]</code>.</p>",
   "answerpreload": "def reset(L):\n    L = []\n\n\n# ---- Use this space to test your function; comment it out before Check ----\n# a = [1, 2]; b = a; reset(a); print(a, b)\n",
   "mark": 1.0,
   "tests": [
    {
     "testcode": "a = [1, 2]\nb = a\nreset(a)\nprint(a, b)",
     "stdin": "",
     "expected": "[] []",
     "extra": "",
     "show": true,
     "example": true,
     "in_precheck": true,
     "in_check": true
    },
    {
     "testcode": "L = []\nreset(L)\nprint(L)",
     "stdin": "",
     "expected": "[]",
     "extra": "",
     "show": true,
     "example": true,
     "in_precheck": false,
     "in_check": true
    },
    {
     "testcode": "L = list(map(int, input().split()))\nM = L\nreset(M)\nprint(L, M)",
     "stdin": "4 5 6",
     "expected": "[] []",
     "extra": "",
     "show": false,
     "example": false,
     "in_precheck": false,
     "in_check": true
    },
    {
     "testcode": "L = list(map(int, input().split()))\nreset(L)\nprint(L, len(L))",
     "stdin": "1 2 3 4 5",
     "expected": "[] 0",
     "extra": "",
     "show": false,
     "example": false,
     "in_precheck": false,
     "in_check": true
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "xml_index": 38,
   "xml_name": "L07_038_Count And Index",
   "display_name": "Count And Index",
   "questiontext_html": "<p>Two methods answer questions about a list without changing it:</p>\n<ul><li><code>L.count(x)</code> returns <b>how many</b> items are equal to <code>x</code> (0 if none);</li><li><code>L.index(x)</code> returns the index of the <b>first</b> item equal to <code>x</code> (a <code>ValueError</code> if there is none, as you saw in Lab 6).</li></ul>\n<pre>L = [&quot;a&quot;, &quot;b&quot;, &quot;a&quot;, &quot;c&quot;, &quot;a&quot;]\nprint(L.count(&quot;a&quot;), L.count(&quot;z&quot;))\nprint(L.index(&quot;c&quot;))\nprint(L.index(&quot;a&quot;))</pre>\n<p>Output:</p>\n<pre>3 0\n3\n0</pre>\n<p><b>Your task:</b> write the function <code>summary(L, x)</code>, which returns a list of two numbers: how many times <code>x</code> appears in the list <code>L</code>, and the index of the first <code>x</code> (or <code>-1</code> if <code>x</code> is not in <code>L</code>).</p>\n<p>For example, <code>summary([\"a\", \"b\", \"a\"], \"a\")</code> returns <code>[2, 0]</code>.</p>",
   "answerpreload": "# Define summary(L, x): return [count of x, index of first x or -1].\n\n\n\n# ---- Use this space to test your function; comment it out before Check ----\n# print(summary([\"a\", \"b\", \"a\"], \"a\"))\n",
   "mark": 1.0,
   "tests": [
    {
     "testcode": "print(summary([\"a\", \"b\", \"a\"], \"a\"))",
     "stdin": "",
     "expected": "[2, 0]",
     "extra": "",
     "show": true,
     "example": true,
     "in_precheck": true,
     "in_check": true
    },
    {
     "testcode": "print(summary([\"a\", \"b\", \"a\"], \"z\"))",
     "stdin": "",
     "expected": "[0, -1]",
     "extra": "",
     "show": true,
     "example": true,
     "in_precheck": false,
     "in_check": true
    },
    {
     "testcode": "print(summary([], 1))",
     "stdin": "",
     "expected": "[0, -1]",
     "extra": "",
     "show": true,
     "example": true,
     "in_precheck": false,
     "in_check": true
    },
    {
     "testcode": "L = list(map(int, input().split()))\nprint(summary(L, 5))",
     "stdin": "1 5 2 5 5",
     "expected": "[3, 1]",
     "extra": "",
     "show": false,
     "example": false,
     "in_precheck": false,
     "in_check": true
