  {
   "xml_index": 41,
   "xml_name": "L07_041_Min Max And Sum",
   "display_name": "Min Max And Sum",
   "questiontext_html": "<p>Python has built-in functions that work on a whole list of numbers:</p>\n<ul><li><code>min(L)</code> and <code>max(L)</code> give the smallest and largest item;</li><li><code>sum(L)</code> gives the total (0 for an empty list);</li><li><code>len(L)</code> gives the number of items.</li></ul>\n<pre>temps = [31, 28, 35, 30]\nprint(min(temps), max(temps))\nprint(sum(temps), len(temps))\nprint(sum(temps) / len(temps))</pre>\n<p>Output:</p>\n<pre>28 35\n124 4\n31.0</pre>\n<p>(<code>min</code> and <code>max</code> of an empty list are errors: there is no smallest item.)</p>\n<p><b>Your task:</b> write the function <code>stats(L)</code>, which returns a list <code>[smallest, largest, average]</code> for a non-empty list of integers <code>L</code>, where the average is rounded to 2 decimal places with <code>round(value, 2)</code>.</p>\n<p>For example, <code>stats([31, 28, 35, 30])</code> returns <code>[28, 35, 31.0]</code>.</p>",
   "answerpreload": "# Define stats(L): return [min, max, average rounded to 2 places].\n\n\n\n# ---- Use this space to test your function; comment it out before Check ----\n# print(stats([31, 28, 35, 30]))\n",
   "mark": 1.0,
   "tests": [
    {
     "testcode": "print(stats([31, 28, 35, 30]))",
     "stdin": "",
     "expected": "[28, 35, 31.0]",
