  {
   "xml_index": 42,
   "xml_name": "L07_042_Remove Duplicates",
   "display_name": "Remove Duplicates",
   "questiontext_html": "<p>The last questions put several ideas together, with less help. Think first about <b>which list tools</b> you need (a new list with <code>append</code>? <code>in</code>? <code>sorted</code>? a slice?), and test your function on small examples, including an <b>empty list</b> and a list with <b>one item</b>.</p>\n<p><b>Your task:</b> write the function <code>unique(L)</code>, which returns a new list with the items of <code>L</code> but without repeats: only the <b>first</b> time each value appears is kept, in the original order. <code>L</code> must not change.</p>\n<p>For example, <code>unique([3, 1, 3, 2, 1])</code> returns <code>[3, 1, 2]</code>.</p>",
   "answerpreload": "# Define unique(L).\n\n\n\n# ---- Use this space to test your function; comment it out before Check ----\n# print(unique([3, 1, 3, 2, 1]))\n",
