   "display_name": "Second Largest",
   "questiontext_html": "<p>The last questions put several ideas together, with less help. Think first about <b>which list tools</b> you need (a new list with <code>append</code>? <code>in</code>? <code>sorted</code>? a slice?), and test your function on small examples, including an <b>empty list</b> and a list with <b>one item</b>.</p>\n<p><b>Your task:</b> write the function <code>second_largest(L)</code>, which returns the second largest <b>different</b> value in the list of integers <code>L</code>. For example, in <code>[5, 9, 9, 7]</code> the largest value is 9 and the second largest different value is 7. <code>L</code> has at least two different values. <code>L</code> must not change.</p>\n<p>For example, <code>second_largest([5, 9, 9, 7])</code> returns <code>7</code>.</p>",
